    "reconstruction_notes": {
      "en": "Trace-concept artistic teaching section: continuous gray host-rock block with a unioned network of stout smooth negative tunnel cavities, two open Y junctions and section-edge outlets. The upper section plane removes the roof to expose the cavity/host relationship; dark inner surfaces are original gray palette, not floating branches, worms or filled casts. Nominal 0.32 m block width, path layout and section convention are art choices. No producer species, exact trace dimensions, behavior, excavated specimen or locality asserted.",
